   "why": "One question, to the architect, and it decides GBP 10,055.76.\n\nThe window schedule carries 3no WN_7 marked AOV and 4no WL_1 'louvres to smoke shaft'. NBS L20 cl.630 specifies both as Colt proprietary smoke-control units, 24V motorised, EN 12101-2. BSW quoted all 7 as plain Sheerline windows - QT252257 has no actuator, motor, control gear, free area or certification anywhere in it, at GBP 413-443/m2, which is plain-window money. Those 7 units are the whole of that quote: GBP 7,085.76 cost, GBP 10,055.76 sell.\n\nSo either they are ours and materially under-priced, or they are the smoke-vent specialist's and that sell comes out. Our proposal names them in the tender information and does neither.\n\nThe 4 louvres may not exist any more. Fire strategy 14003-14005 rev 09.10.2025: 'SMOKE SHAFT OMITTED'. Never reversed through rev 04-06 of 17.02.2026. The window schedule (08.09.2025) and the NBS (23.08.2025) both predate that and neither was ever revised - which is why they still show it.\n\nIt goes to ARKON, not Chigwell: no fire engineer, fire consultant or approved inspector is named anywhere on this job, so the fire strategy and the NBS are the architect's own work. Arkon Associates, job 5244, enquiries@arkonassociates.co.uk.\n\nFree area is written geometric throughout the pack, so the aerodynamic-vs-geometric trap does not bite here.\n\nFull evidence: data/request-detail/REQ-22.md",
