   "sent": "2026-08-04 12:50 BST",
   "to": "adam",
   "subject": "Redditch QUOTE TO CHECK - do not send yet. BSW are 30% under my benchmark, but GBP 9,641 of scope is missing and BSW have not priced the spec",
   "body": "Adam,\n Gintare's quote is with you at GBP 79,912.22 and she has asked whether to send a full\nproposal. Not yet. Three things missing from it have rates; five more are missing from BSW's\nquote and have none.\n The good news first, and it is real.\n BSW CAME IN AT GBP 43,739.72 AND MY BENCHMARK WAS 30% HIGH\n I had BSW frames at GBP 56,993.38. They have quoted GBP 43,739.72 - GBP 13,253.66 less. That\nis my error, not a keen price: the Severn Trent curve I built it from was 3005 Wine Red\nmetallic and this quote is stock white. I flagged that caveat on 28/07; it turns out to be\nworth most of the gap.\n It matters because my GBP 94,926.76 was built on a frame price that does not exist. On BSW's\nreal one this job is winnable.\n WHAT IS MISSING AND HAS A RATE - GBP 9,641.31\n W36 - BSW quoted Qty: 1 against &quot;w35,36&quot; 1,481.86\nits installation 160.00\nstrip out, 43 nr x 150 - your 28/07 ruling, and Joedan cl.12 6,450.00\nperimeter sealing - pack p70 cl.11 REQUIRES it, and it sits\non the document as an OPTIONAL extra 1,549.45\n---------\n9,641.31\n 79,912.22 + 9,641.31 = GBP 89,553.53, or GBP 91,849.77 with your 2.5% MCD.\n Against Joedan's GBP 90,687.17 on the same basis that is GBP 1,163 ABOVE him - not the\nGBP 10,775 below that GBP 79,912.22 looks like.\n W36 IS BSW'S DROP AND IT WENT STRAIGHT THROUGH. Every other multi-reference line on their\nquote carries the right count (w1,w2 = 2, w22,23 = 2, w16-18 = 3, w24-28 = 5). One line is\nwrong and it is the only one. Their own footer says they &quot;will not be held responsible for\nany items missing from quotes&quot;, so it is ours to catch.\n WHAT BSW HAVE NOT PRICED AT ALL - all five were asked for in writing, all push the price up\n 1. SOLAR CONTROL GLASS. The RFQ asked for &quot;outer pane 4mm bronze anti sun&quot;. All 68 panes are\n 6.8 Lam / 18 / 4mm CLEAR. Not one instance of anti-sun, bronze, solar or tint in twelve\n pages. The tender requires it; I carry GBP 1,814.51 for the premium.\n 2. THE DOOR IRONMONGERY. The RFQ asked for Axim 8800 concealed closers, PR7100 exit panic\n devices, flush bolts to slave leaves and anti-finger-trap stiles on doors 32/34/37/41. BSW\n have quoted Ultion key cylinders, Prolinea lever handles and a Standard Resi Lock - a\n domestic front door - on fire escape doors in a public library. Zero instances of &quot;panic&quot;\n in the quote. Georgie's, again.\n 3. WINDOW RESTRICTORS, 100mm. Asked for. Not one unit has them; 17 units open.\n 4. COLOUR. All 29 items are stock 9910HG Hipca White. The RFQ says &quot;standard RAL colour (not\n confirmed)&quot;. A RAL finish is an uplift.\n 5. DELIVERY. Their terms are ex works.\n\n Also worth knowing before anyone reads the elevations: BSW note &quot;some transoms have been\nadded due to sash size limits&quot;. They have put extra transoms across several units, and they\nhave quoted refs 16/17/18 as flat 2250 x 2304 rectangles when the drawing shows them raked to\nthe stair soffit. Both are live RFIs and neither is settled.\n THE PROPOSAL SHOULD NOT GO AS DRAFTED, SEPARATELY FROM THE PRICE\n - IT CERTIFIES U-VALUE 1.4 W/m2K. BSW's quote states no whole-window U-value anywhere.\n&quot;EcoPlus 1.0&quot; is a centre-pane Ug, not a Uw. Filwood this morning and Georgie's last week\nwere the same shape: a performance figure on the face of our document that the supplier's\nown quote does not support.\n- The glazing box reads &quot;6.8mm laminated / 4mm toughened&quot; - accurate to BSW, and silent on\nthe solar control the tender asks for. If the glass stays clear that has to be a stated\ndeviation, not a gap.\n- &quot;External mastic is charged as an optional extra&quot; - third job running.\n- STRIP OUT APPEARS NOWHERE, not in inclusions and not in exclusions, while &quot;Waste Removal -\ngenerally excluded&quot; does. On 43 metal-framed openings that reads badly whichever way a QS\ntakes it.\n- Working hours are stated as 07:30-16:30. The tender says 08:30-17:30 in the prelims and\n08:30-18:00 in the Schedule of Works, it is an occupied public library, and windows cannot\nbe left out over a shift.\n- It promises a full-time CSCS/SMSTS site supervisor, a dedicated project manager AND a\nseparate contracts manager. Installation is GBP 8,410 and recomputes to GBP 7,420 of\nfit-only labour, so there is GBP 990 standing behind all of that.\n- THE TEN YEAR WARRANTY IS ONLY IN THE BACK-PAGE T&Cs. Joedan give twelve months. On a 70/30\nprice/quality award it belongs in the summary and the inclusions - it is the one place we\nbeat him, and we are not going to beat him on price.\n AND DO NOT SEND THE .XLSX. It still carries the working columns - &quot;Supplier used: BSW\n43,739.72&quot; in K3/M3 and our frame cost per line in J and P. Anyone who opens it and scrolls\nright reads our buy and our 38.8% margin. Both files also carry Nicholas Baker as author,\ndan.parker@agsurveying.co.uk, and links into two other people's Outlook caches. That is\nREQ-27 and I am not re-raising it - scripts\\clean_issued_pack.py strips all of it and these\nfiles were never run through it.\n WHAT I WOULD DO\n 1. Back to BSW today with the five omissions. Their quote is dated 04/08 and holds thirty days.\n 2. Add W36, strip out and sealing now - they have rates and they are not in dispute.\n 3. Issue nothing to Leonard until BSW's gaps come back. Every one of them is upward, and he\n has been holding &quot;around 89k&quot; since 29/07.\n\n Mary Grace\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
