   "body": "Adam,\n The &quot;around GBP 89k&quot; you gave Leonard White at 11:14 today is the 28/07 figure. The live\ntender sum is GBP 94,926.76 - GBP 5,708.11 higher, and it is the number in the documents\nsitting with you now.\n Nothing has gone to Pride from me, so the only thing Leonard holds is your indication. It\nis still cheap to correct. It stops being cheap when the formal quote lands.\n FIRST, WHICH WAS IT\n GBP 89k matches our 28/07 pricing document exactly - GBP 89,218.65.\nI sent you GBP 93,526.34 at 10:04 this morning, and GBP 94,926.76 at 11:42.\nYour 11:30 reply came off the 28/07 thread, whose subject line still carries 89,218.65.\n If you indicated low on purpose to hold Pride's interest, then the question is only how we\nfund it and the rest of this email is the price list. If you were working off the old\nthread, it needs correcting today. I cannot tell from here which it was, so I am not\nassuming.\n WHERE THE GBP 5,708.11 WENT - ALL OF IT, AND NONE OF IT A RE-PRICE\n strip-out at the real rate, 43 nr x GBP 150.00,\nreplacing the GBP 3,000 allowance we guessed on 28/07 3,538.46\ncode adders - the 125% rule above 6 m2, refs 19 and 20 769.23\nframes - the supplier factors were hardcoded in my script\nand had moved overnight; they now read live from source 1,400.42\n----------\n5,708.11\n All gross of the 2.5% MCD, same basis as everything else on this job. Two of those three\nare corrections I made and told you about; the third is a guess replaced by Fenster's own\nBrandon Estate rate. Nothing in it is a change of mind about the scope.\n THE PART THAT COSTS MORE THAN THE MONEY\n GBP 89,218.65 is GBP 1,468.52 UNDER Joedan's GBP 90,687.17.\nGBP 94,926.76 is GBP 4,239.59 OVER it.\n Leonard has now been told in writing that we are the cheaper bid, and asked to say how it\ncompares against the other returns. The formal quote moves us from 1.6% under to 4.7%\nover on a number he is actively benchmarking. That swing is what does the damage, more\nthan the GBP 5,708 does.\n IF YOU DECIDE TO HOLD THE GBP 89k\n Sell fixes on submission, so what moves is margin:\n margin % of net\nlive, GBP 94,926.76 20,625.00 22.3%\nheld at GBP 89,218.65 15,059.59 17.3%\nheld at 89,218.65, buying BSW 12,488.87 14.4%\n BSW is the only supplier anybody has actually asked. So the realistic version of honouring\nthat indication is GBP 12,489 - thinner than the worst supplier case I sized for you\nyesterday (GBP 16,689, 18.3%), and still gross of prelims we do not charge at all and a\nfitting cost that is recorded nowhere.\n WHAT I WOULD DO\n Correct it to Leonard now, before the formal quote, on the strip-out. It is true, it is\nGBP 3,538 of the GBP 5,708, it is a rate replacing an allowance rather than a price rise,\nand today it costs nothing. A QS mid-comparison who gets a 6.4% increase without warning\ndiscounts both numbers, not just the second one.\n Your call, not mine - if you would rather absorb it and hold GBP 89k, the table above is\nwhat that buys.\n ONE THING IN THE EMAIL ITSELF\n &quot;The same inclusions/exclusions as the other subcontractor's quote details&quot; is right on\nall 11 inclusions and 25 exclusions - I lifted them verbatim from Joedan's own lists at\npack p151-153. There is one deliberate difference: our TEN YEAR guarantee against their\ntwelve months.\n On a 70/30 price/quality award where we are now the dearer bid, that guarantee is the only\nplace this bid can be won. I would not describe our offer to Leonard as the same as\nJoedan's. It is already on the face of the proposal, in the summary and in the inclusions.\n THE DEADLINE - YOU HAVE ASKED IT\n &quot;When are you submitting cost on this one?&quot; is the question that has been open on this job\nsince 28/07, and you have now put it to the person who can answer it. Nothing further from\nme on that; I will pick his answer up when it lands and I am not raising it again.\n Mary Grace\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
