   "to": "adam",
   "subject": "Trafalgar House - Michael Beyer asked two questions on 14/07 and the quote he is chasing answers neither",
   "body": "Adam,\n Paul chased Michael Beyer on Trafalgar House at 11:54 today. Before anyone gets a reply -\nhe asked us two specific questions on 14 July and neither is answered in the quotation he\nis being chased about.\n Our number is GBP 71,566.47 + VAT, issued 22/07, Liniar uPVC via TruFrame.\n WHAT HE ASKED, 14 JULY 12:31\n &quot;We don't have a spec at present, so best guess on the requirements regarding glass,\nplease can you state what your allowance achieves so we can provide this to them as\npart of the budget costs.&quot;\n &quot;They have also asked for replacement costs for the doors which we also don't have a\nspec for, so please allow for standard ironmongery etc and provide info on your\nallowance.&quot;\n He is preparing a tender and has to hand our allowances to HIS client. That is the whole\nreason he asked.\n 1. THE GLASS PERFORMANCE - NOBODY HAS IT, INCLUDING US\n Our proposal states the make-up: 4/20/4 clear toughened soft coat, argon filled, black\nwarm edge spacer. It never states what that achieves. No U-value, no W/m2K, no energy\nrating anywhere in the document.\n And we cannot answer it from the file either. TruFrame's own glass order carries the\nsentence built for exactly this:\n &quot;With the specification of glass defined below, you can expect the window on this job\nto achieve a WER **********&quot;\n The rating prints as ten asterisks. Whether that means it was never calculated or is a\nprint artefact is a question for TruFrame - either way no figure was produced, and a blank\nin a supplier document reads as boilerplate rather than as a gap, which is why it went\nunnoticed.\n So this one needs a call to TruFrame before we can answer him.\n 2. THE IRONMONGERY - WE DID HAVE IT AND DID NOT PASS IT ON\n This one is only a copying job. TruFrame's quotation sheet 10213105 specifies handles,\nhandle heights, hinges, hinge quantities and cylinders line by line.\n The word &quot;ironmongery&quot; does not appear in our proposal at all. The only hardware reference\nis &quot;shootbolt locking, panic hardware where required&quot; in the executive summary, which is a\nlocking note, not the allowance he asked for.\n WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS\n It is a budget price with no specification. When the real spec arrives, an allowance we\nnever stated is an allowance we cannot point back to - so any upgrade becomes an argument\nrather than a variation. Answering both now, while he is actively asking, costs nothing.\nIt gets harder the moment he has passed our figure upward.\n SEPARATELY - THE DOCUMENT TRACES REACHED A THIRD CLIENT\n Same problem as Filwood and Georgie's. Topek Southern hold:\n Proposal PDF - author &quot;Nicholas Baker&quot;\nPricing XLSX - &quot;Dan Parker&quot;, &quot;dan.parker&quot;, &quot;agsurveying&quot;, plus external links\npointing at other people's Outlook cache folders\n Not a new issue and I am not raising it again - Filwood already owns the fix, which is to\nclean the master template once. Recording it only because three clients now hold documents\nnaming a third party, which is a fair argument for doing that sooner. scripts\\clean_issued_pack.py\nalready strips all of it; these files were simply never run through it.\n Mary Grace\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
