   "subject": "Redditch REASSESSED - the live number is GBP 93,526.34, NOT the 89,218.65 in this subject line. Documents attached, dated today, ready to send",
   "body": "Adam,\n Reassessed. Attached are the pricing document and proposal, rebuilt and dated today, ready to go.\n FIRST - THE NUMBER IN YOUR SUBJECT LINE IS DEAD. DO NOT SUBMIT GBP 89,218.65.\n That figure was superseded at 09:12 this morning. The live number is:\n TENDER SUM GBP 93,526.34 gross of 2.5% MCD, excluding VAT\n The change was the strip-out line. On Monday night it was a GBP 3,000 guess because no rate existed.\nREQ-24 then produced a real one - our own Brandon Estate tender to Elkins prices removal of existing\nframes at GBP 150.00 per unit, identical to the penny across both revisions as that job nearly\ndoubled in size. 43 units is GBP 6,450. The rest of the rise is GBP 750 of code adders after another\njob measured that we charge 125% above 6 m2, not 75%, which affects refs 19 and 20 here.\n I have re-run everything against the current engine this morning as you asked. Nothing has moved\nsince 09:12 - that reassessment is the one you are asking for, and it is already in the attached.\n SECOND - WE ARE NOT SENDING OUT A CHEAPER QUOTE\n You wrote that we have nothing to lose sending out a cheaper quote. I would agree if we were, but we\nare not. At GBP 93,526.34 we are GBP 2,839.17 ABOVE Joedan's GBP 90,687.17 - 3.13% above, on the\nsame basis, both gross of the same 2.5% discount.\n I would rather you knew that before you pressed send than after Gleeds tabulated it.\n YOUR INSTINCT ABOUT JOEDAN IS RIGHT AND IT IS MEASURABLE\n They are a manufacturer, and that is exactly the gap. EL75mm Squareline and AC100 Commercial are\nJoedan's own products - they are not buying a frame from anybody. We are. Our frame buy on this job\nis GBP 53,057 and our margin is GBP 20,625, so 22.6% of our sell is the margin sitting on top of a\nframe that our competitor fabricates in his own factory.\n That is a structural difference and no amount of sharpening our end closes it. It is why we came out\nabove them even when the strip-out line was still a guess.\n THIRD - WHAT SUBMITTING BEFORE THE SUPPLIER QUOTE ACTUALLY COSTS\n You are right that we cannot wait, and I want to give you the size of that risk rather than just\nflag it. It is smaller than I made it sound yesterday.\n The sell is fixed the moment we submit. What moves is our margin when the real frame price lands:\n if the quote comes back at... frame buy margin left % of net\nBSW - the only one asked 56,993.38 16,688.84 18.3%\nAplus - what the price assumes 53,057.22 20,625.00 22.6%\n4Ali 53,111.14 20,571.08 22.6%\nTruFrame 44,268.27 29,413.95 32.3%\n So the worst realistic case is that we earn GBP 16,689 instead of GBP 20,625. Thinner, not a loss.\nThat is a risk worth taking to hit a deadline.\n The honest caveat on those figures: that is GROSS margin. It carries no prelims, no site supervision,\nno survey and no project management - Brandon's document charges 4.2% of works for exactly those and\nours charges nothing - and what fitting actually costs Fenster is recorded nowhere I can see.\n AND THE ONE CLAUSE THAT NOW WORKS IN OUR FAVOUR\n Yesterday I flagged that our standard terms hold a quotation for 30 days while this tender wants the\nsum open 10 weeks, and called it a compliance problem. Today it is the opposite. If we submit a\nbenchmark price before the supplier quotes land, that 30-day clause is the only thing capping how\nlong we are exposed on it.\n So it is a live choice rather than a fault: hold to the tender's 10 weeks to 3 months and be fully\ncompliant but exposed for all of it, or submit on our 30 days and be qualified but protected. You\ncannot have both, and I would take the 30 days on a price built this way.\n WHAT I WOULD DO\n Submit at GBP 93,526.34 on 30-day validity. Then get the RFQ to Aplus, 4Ali and TruFrame today, not\njust BSW - I sent you that schedule separately and it is the only thing that can bring the number\ndown. On the measured factors TruFrame is the only one of the four that clears Joedan, and if their\nquote lands inside 30 days your retroactive sense check arrives while we can still act on it rather\nthan after we are committed.\n And on the 70/30 award: if we cannot win on price, the 30% is where this bid has to work. Our ten\nyear guarantee against Joedan's twelve months is on the face of the proposal, in the summary and in\nthe inclusions, because it is the one thing we are clearly better at here.\n WHAT YOU WOULD BE UNDERWRITING, STATED PLAINLY\n Since this is the first Mary-only quote, you should know exactly which parts are evidence and which\nare not. Quantities, configurations and areas are from the client's own schedule, checked line by\nline against the elevations. Strip-out, the code adders, installation and the solar glass are house\nrates. The frame supply is a BENCHMARK - a curve fitted to BSW's real quote for Pride's Severn Trent\njob, adjusted to a second supplier. No supplier has quoted this job. mary_checks passes on every\nrule, and the client copy carries no cost columns and no third-party file properties.\n Nothing has gone to Pride. Still no deadline from Leonard White, which is the other thing worth\nchasing while this goes out.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
