   "subject": "Redditch: the RFQ went to BSW only, and BSW is the one supplier that cannot beat Joedan - please send the attached to Aplus, 4Ali, TruFrame and SBM",
   "body": "Adam,\n Short one, because there is a decision in it that is worth making this morning rather than tomorrow.\n The Redditch RFQ went to BSW at 11:19. Good - it needed to move. But BSW is the one supplier that\ncannot win this job for us, and if we wait for their quote and stop there, the answer will look like\n&quot;Redditch is not winnable&quot; when what it actually says is &quot;we asked the dearest supplier&quot;.\n Our GBP 93,526.34 already assumes an Aplus-level buy. A BSW quote comes back above that. Using the\nsupplier factors measured off our own sent pricing documents, same code and band:\n supplier frame buy tender sum vs Joedan's 90,687.17\nBSW - the only one asked 56,993.38 97,563.42 +6,876 ABOVE\nAplus - what we assumed 53,057.22 93,526.34 +2,839 above\n4Ali 53,111.14 93,581.64 +2,894 above\nTruFrame 44,268.27 84,512.03 -6,175 UNDER\n Two things fall out of that. BSW is nearly GBP 3,936 of frame buy dearer than the price we have\nalready published internally. And TruFrame is the only one of the four whose measured level clears\nJoedan - by GBP 6,175, which would also pay for the prelims I flagged yesterday.\n I am not telling you TruFrame will do it. That factor is -17.9% on n=42, the thinnest of the four\nsamples, and nothing in it proves they can fabricate a thermally broken 75mm commercial system with\npanic-hardware doorsets at this size. It proves it is worth asking, and asking is free.\n WHAT I AM ASKING FOR: send the attached to Aplus, 4Ali, TruFrame and SBM as well. It is the\nprice-free RFQ schedule - no rates, no margin, no competitor's number in it - and it already asks\nfor refs 32 and 34 as single coupled units in one depth, states the trickle vents and the panic\nironmongery, flags the raked units and ref 38, and asks them to state their validity against a\n10-week tender. I cannot send it myself. One email each and we would know by the end of the week\nwhether this job is winnable or not.\n ONE OBSERVATION, AND IT MAY ALREADY BE STALE. As at 11:21, ninety seconds after it left, the copy\nof the BSW email in our records carries no attachment while the text says &quot;as per the attached&quot;.\nNinety seconds is not long enough to conclude anything - the same flag on Georgie's yesterday was\nright on the evidence and wrong about the world by a minute - so please read this as &quot;worth a\nglance&quot;, not as a mistake. The store does record attachments on our sent mail, 31 of 110, so the\nzero is real evidence rather than a gap in the record.\n The part of it that is not time-sensitive: whatever does go to BSW should be the RFQ schedule and\nnot the tender pack. Joedan's fully priced quotation is sitting at page 147 of that pack. Sending it\nto a supplier tells them exactly what the job is worth before they price it for us.\n Nothing has gone to Pride. Still waiting on their real deadline from Leonard White.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
