   "body": "Adam,\n One correction to the email I sent you an hour ago, and then the two enquiries ready to go.\n THE REPLY TO BSW ALREADY WENT, AND IT WAS EMPTY\n Estimating replied to BSW at 10:54 this morning, thirteen minutes after their answer. The message has no text in it at all - no question, no signature, nothing. It is BSW's own email quoted back, byte for byte, with an Outlook header on top. No attachment.\n So none of the four open points were chased, and BSW have a blank email from us sitting thirteen minutes after they told us they had left the panic bars out. From their side that reads as &quot;received, no objection&quot;. On a fire exit I would rather it did not.\n Not a one-off, and this is the bit worth knowing: of 108 emails sent from our addresses in my records, four carry no message text. Three of them are from this morning. Two went to Neil Macilwaine at Pearce on Georgie's, at 09:03 and 09:16. I have passed that to the Georgie's side separately.\n ENQUIRY 1 - TO BSW, ready to send\n Hi,\n Thanks for the revised quote. Four things please:\n 1. What does the Casement Restrictor Stay restrict the opening to? The drawing calls for 250mm.\n\n 2. The drawing puts the restriction on site - &quot;Friction hinges - screw inserted on site to\n restrict to 250mm&quot;. If that is the intent, do we still need the stays, or should they come\n back out?\n\n 3. Your uPVC quote QT252647 included a 4000 External Linkvent on all eight frames. QT253300 has\n no vent on any of the seven. Is that deliberate?\n\n 4. Handles are quoted as Signature Handle White. The drawing schedules SAA espag locking handles\n - satin anodised aluminium. Can you supply SAA, and what is the difference?\n\n And the question from Monday that is still open: can you supply W.01, W.04 and W.05 in SMA Smart\nWall so they couple to the doors, or does that have to come from elsewhere?\n ENQUIRY 2 - TO BELLVIEW, ready to send, and this is the one nobody has sent yet\n Hi,\n Wexham Primary SEND Facility, against your 0000000475. Four things please:\n 1. Does your price for ED.02, the rear double doors, include a panic / push bar? The drawing\n requires fire exit hardware on the internal side including an SAA push bar which overrides\n any locking mechanism installed.\n\n 2. BSW have raised that the Europrofile hook lock the drawing also calls for cannot be released\n by a push bar. Can SMA supply a fire exit device compatible with the hook lock on this leaf,\n or does the locking have to change? A written answer please - it is a fire exit.\n\n 3. ED.01: the drawing schedules SAA 300mm 'D' handles and a concealed overhead HOLD OPEN closer.\n Please confirm both are in your price.\n\n 4. Please price W.01 (2424 x 2400, coupled to ED.01) and W.04 / W.05 (869 x 2400, flanking\n ED.02) as Smart Wall elements. Ideally as complete assemblies - East run 1212+1212+1227,\n West run 869+1872+869, both 2400 high.\n\n Item 4 is the rebuild. Until it comes back the pricing document cannot be corrected.\n Nothing else has changed since my earlier email, and I have not put anything on the board.\n Mary\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
