   "to": "adam",
   "subject": "Manor Lodge Q7666 - the escape question is answered by the client's own spec, and one thing to watch on Rev C",
   "body": "Adam,\n Closing my own loop on the email I sent you at 10:13, and one thing to watch on the next\nrevision. Still not re-opening Manor Lodge - it is Steve's and it is a live project.\n 1. THE ESCAPE QUESTION IS ANSWERED - BY THE CLIENT, NOT BY AFS\n Steve wrote to Julian at 10:46, 33 minutes after my email, with the client's own spec:\n &quot;Mag Lock, Push to Exit, Green Break-glass and external reader to be fitted to Exit\ndoor R-024&quot;\n The client is fitting their own maglock, so the access control and the escape release are\ntheir package, not AFS's. That takes the whole panic bar / panic pad problem out of AFS's\nscope - which is why it was never going to be answered from that direction.\n So point 3 of my earlier email is superseded rather than wrong. It was accurate at 10:13.\nI would rather tell you that than leave you thinking there is an open safety question on a\nschool escape door when there is not.\n 2. WHAT TO WATCH ON REV C\n Steve has asked AFS to remove the EFF EFF electric strike and &quot;re-issue with a saving&quot;.\n On this same quotation, the last deletion produced no saving at all. The PLANET roller\nblind came out between Rev A and Rev B and the net stayed at GBP 4,075.02 to the penny.\n The quotation carries no component breakdown - it is one line for the whole door - so\nnobody can say what the strike is worth. The only check available is whether the total\nmoves at all. If Rev C comes back at GBP 4,075.02 again, that is now twice.\n 3. THE RE-ISSUE IS A FREE CHANCE TO CLEAR THE OTHER TWO\n Rev C has to be produced anyway, so it costs nothing to ask Julian at the same time:\n - why the PLANET external protective roller blind was deleted, and whether it should\nreturn\n- whether the DR. HAHN hinges are meant to be Anodised now rather than Anthracite grey\nmatt, given the door is RAL 7021 matt\n Both changed at Rev B without being asked for and without being mentioned.\n Mary Grace\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
