   "subject": "Manor Lodge Q7666 Rev B - swing fixed, but a part was deleted at the same price and the escape question is still unanswered",
   "body": "Adam,\n AFS issued Manor Lodge Q7666 Rev B this morning at 10:06. It does fix the thing it was\nasked to fix - but two other things changed with it, and the price did not move.\n Not re-opening this one. You ruled on 28/07 that Manor Lodge is a live project and\nJoseph's when he exists. This is just what the document says, for whoever places the order.\n 1. WHAT REV B CORRECTLY FIXES\n Steve told AFS at 14:52 yesterday that the door opens OUT, hinged right. Rev A said inward.\n Rev B now reads &quot;outward opening Right Hinged&quot;. Correct.\n 2. TWO CHANGES NOBODY ASKED FOR, AT AN IDENTICAL PRICE\n I diffed the Rev A and Rev B parts lists. Beyond the swing, two things moved:\n - DELETED: &quot;PLANET - External protective roller blinds, L=1925 mm, Anthracite grey\n(Satin)&quot;, 1 off. Present in Rev A, absent from Rev B.\n - CHANGED: the DR. HAHN roller hinges go from &quot;Anthracite grey (Matt)&quot; to &quot;Anodised&quot;.\nThe door is RAL 7021 matt, so the hinges no longer match the frame colour.\n Both revisions are GBP 4,075.02 net, to the penny.\n I am not assuming that is an error. Deleting an item may well be correct on an\noutward-opening leaf - but it was not part of what Steve asked for, it is not mentioned in\nJulian's covering email, and a component has left the quotation without the price changing.\nWorth one question to AFS before it is ordered.\n 3. STEVE'S ESCAPE QUESTION IS STILL UNANSWERED - THIRD TIME\n He asked on 28/07 at 09:11: &quot;Can you confirm if the panic gear is required if we have a\npush to exit option?&quot;\n AFS have replied three times since - 10:40, 13:33 and this morning - and have answered the\nmaglock and the swing but never that.\n Meanwhile AFS have said in writing, twice, that they cannot supply either option: no push\nbar at 900mm (they need 920mm minimum) and no panic pad at all, it is not in their\nsupplier's range.\n So Rev B contains neither of the two things Steve was choosing between. Internal operation\nis a thumbturn, with an EFF EFF electric strike for the access control. The lock is an ECO\nSCHULTE GBS70 and the quotation does not state whether it is panic-rated.\n He originally asked for the bar on 24/07 because &quot;this door needs to be used for escape\npurpose as well&quot;, and this is a school. Whether a thumbturn satisfies that is a question for\nsomeone qualified to answer it - my point is only that nobody has answered it, and the\nrevision in Steve's hands does not resolve it either way.\n 4. NUMBERS, FOR THE ORDER\n Net, supply only, delivered to site GBP 4,075.02\nFixing pack (optional extra) GBP 75.21\nDelivery (optional extra) GBP 250.00\nTrue delivered cost GBP 4,400.23\n The fixing pack and delivery sit OUTSIDE the net figure - the same shape as Gordon Court's\nGBP 506.37. Anyone reading GBP 4,075.02 as the delivered cost is GBP 325.21 light.\n Validity is 30 days from 29/07, so 28/08/2026. Lead time 8 weeks from signed order and the\n60% initial payment. Delivery address on the quote is Rectory Lane, Ridge Hill, Radlett,\nHertfordshire WD7 9BG.\n Mary Grace\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
