   "subject": "Redditch Library - nobody has picked it up, the pack's deadline was 26 June, and Appendix 2 is Joedan's own priced quote at GBP 90,687.17",
   "body": "No, estimating have not picked it up. It is on nobody's log and it has been sitting six days.\n I have opened it as a job and the take-off is running now. Four things you will want before it lands.\n 1. IT IS NOT ON THE ESTIMATING LOG AT ALL\n Zero rows for Redditch across all 349 on the log. Pride Developments themselves are well represented - fourteen rows, Peckham Pulse, Severn Trent, Usk House, St Catherines - so this is a live client whose enquiry simply never got logged.\n It came in to info@ on 22 July, Kerry forwarded it to Commercial@ and to you the same afternoon, and nothing happened for six days.\n That is the third one this week that reached us only through info@. John North Hall was the same, and it only got seen because Perry forwarded it by hand.\n 2. THE DATE IN THE PACK IS NOT OUR DEADLINE - AND IT HAS ALREADY PASSED\n\n The Gleeds invitation says returns by 12 noon on Friday 26th June 2026. That is Gleeds' date to the main contractors, and it went a month ago.\n Ours is whatever Pride need. Leonard White asked us on 22/07 to acknowledge and return &quot;asap&quot; and gave no date.\n So the urgency is real but it is Pride's urgency, not a published deadline. Worth one call to Leonard to ask when he actually needs it - if his own submission is already in, we may have more room than &quot;asap&quot; suggests, and if it is not, we need to know that today.\n One thing to hold onto: the Form of Tender requires the price to stay open for 10 WEEKS from submission. Our supplier quotes run 30 days. Same gap as John North Hall's 90-day Section 20 requirement.\n 3. THE PACK CONTAINS A COMPETITOR'S FULLY PRICED SCHEDULE\n Appendix 2, which Leonard pointed us at, is not a specification. It is Joedan Commercial Division's own quotation to Gleeds - quote JCQ.9727, dated 23 March 2026 - left in the tender pack complete with rates.\n 43 items, every one with a size, a configuration, a unit rate and an extended cost.\n GRAND TOTAL: GBP 90,687.17 ex VAT, gross of 2.5% main contractor's discount.\n Their spec is EL75mm Squareline thermally broken aluminium windows and AC100 Commercial non-thermal doors, argon double glazing with warm edge, 1.4 W/m2K area weighted on the windows and 3.0 on the doors.\n That gives us the take-off and the competition in one document. I have told the job chat to price ours independently first and only then compare, because it is very easy to anchor to somebody else's number.\n Their exclusions are worth your eye too: no scaffolding or access equipment of any kind, no skips, no containers, no Building Control, no asbestos removal, no mag locks, no manifestations, and no up-stand where the windows sit onto the flat roof. They include strip-out and put disposal on the main contractor, which is our house position exactly.\n They offer a 12-month warranty. We offer ten years.\n 4. WHAT IS NOT OURS\n The pack is flat roof refurbishment AND windows and doors. Appendix 1 is Alumasc roofing - not our package. We price windows and doors only and say so on the face of the quote.\n There is a refurbishment and demolition asbestos survey at Appendix 3 which needs reading before anyone prices strip-out.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
