   "body": "Adam,\n Unit 1 Eleanor Trade Centre. Your Liniar point is answered and closed, but the quote that went\nout at 13:22 has landed in an empty inbox and it is missing a document it refers to.\n TWO THINGS THAT NEED A PERSON, AND ONE SEND FIXES BOTH.\n 1. MARK GOLDEN IS OUT OF OFFICE. His auto-reply came back at 13:23, one minute after Gintare's\n quote went to him. It has no return date. It says: new enquiries and current projects to\n DAVID PITCHER and JAY TAYLOR, admin and payments to info@bradfordwatts.co.uk, or the office\n on 01992 657555. The quote went to mgolden@ only, copied to you - so nobody at Bradford Watts\n knows it exists. They are on the Priority Customer list, and JLL want this finished by the end\n of September.\n\n 2. THE QUOTATION SAYS TO READ IT WITH TERMS AND CONDITIONS THAT ARE NOT IN IT.\n The last line of the pricing document reads &quot;This pricing document should be read in\n conjunction with the Terms and Conditions.&quot; The workbook has one sheet. There are no terms in\n it, and the email carried nothing else except the drawings.\n\n This is not a Gintare slip, it is the template. The old one - &quot;Pricing Doc 23.03.2026.xlsx&quot; -\nhad four sheets: Cover Letter, Quotation, Drawings, Terms & Conditions. The current\nMASTER PRICING DOC has one sheet, &quot;Pricing Document&quot;, and it still carries that sentence on\nits face. I searched the whole Commercial archive for a standalone Fenster T&Cs file to attach\ninstead - there isn't one. Every &quot;terms and conditions&quot; document in there belongs to a supplier\nor a main contractor. So the terms exist only inside the old template.\n On this job that is not academic. Mark wrote &quot;IF YOU ALLOW the following measurements&quot;. Nothing\nhas been measured, and we have never seen the JLL ground floor plans the new fenestration is\nsupposed to match. The one sentence that protects us is T&C clause 2 - &quot;All quotations are\nsubject to final site survey and measurement verification&quot; - and it is in the document the\nclient does not have. Same for the 30-day validity, the 50% deposit, and retention of title.\n Bradford Watts did get our terms in April, on this same project, because the April quote used\nthe old template. But the July quote is a new offer.\n So: when the quote is re-sent to Pitcher or Taylor, send the terms with it. That is one action\nthat fixes both problems.\n YOUR LINIAR POINT - ANSWERED, NOTHING TO DO.\nYou were reading BSW's own quote. QT252983 dated 20/07 is headed &quot;LINIAR PVCu&quot; and the item under\nit is a SHEERLINE Prestige Casement. Their template header, not the product. The price settles it:\nGBP 462.80 a window against a Liniar uPVC benchmark of about GBP 193/m2 and a Sheerline benchmark\nof about GBP 495/m2. That is an aluminium buy. Gintare's document was corrected before it went and\nreads &quot;Sheerline Aluminium Window&quot;. I also checked the drawing pack we sent the client, text and\nraw file both - no &quot;LINIAR&quot;, no supplier name, no prices, nothing of BSW's or Bellview's in it.\nClean.\n THE QUESTION THAT IS COMING BACK, WORTH HAVING READY.\nApril: GBP 4,252.16 for six uPVC windows, ground and first floor, the whole elevation.\nJuly: GBP 7,975.85 for four aluminium windows and a door, ground floor only.\nThey asked for a REDUCED package and the number nearly doubled. It is right, but somebody will ask.\nThe reason in one line: the windows changed from uPVC to aluminium, GBP 244/m2 to GBP 875/m2, and\nthe GBP 3,334.65 entrance door did not exist in April at all. Strip the door out and the window\nmoney is GBP 3,501.20 against GBP 1,833.09 for the three ground-floor uPVC windows it replaces.\n EIGHT DAYS OF UNCOVERED PRICE. Both supplier quotes are dated 20/07 and both hold for thirty days,\nso BSW QT252983 and Bellview 0000000491 expire on 19/08. Our own validity runs thirty days from\nissue, to 27/08. That is eight days where we are committed and GBP 3,685.85 of buy is not. Worth a\nprice hold from BSW if this drags, and it will drag, because the man who has to accept it is away.\n REQ-27 - THIS ONE IS STILL HAPPENING, NOT HISTORY. The pricing document that went to Bradford Watts\nfive hours ago carries dan.parker@agsurveying.co.uk as its author, both external links to the\nOutlook caches on Liam O'Donnell's and Parke's machines, 50 defined names from electrical and\nstructural steel, and 202 cached values from those workbooks. So does the April quote to the same\nclient. That is the seventh and eighth affected documents, and the seventh is today's. I have added\nit to REQ-27 rather than raising anything new - it is the same file and the same five minutes of\nwork, and the missing Terms & Conditions sheet is a second defect in that same template, so both\nget fixed in one pass.\n SMALLER, FOR WHOEVER PLACES THE ORDER, NOT FOR NOW.\n- BSW state the EXTERNAL colour only, &quot;7016M Anthracite Grey - M&quot;. The internal face is nowhere on\nthe quote. Bellview describe the door only as &quot;Anthracite Grey&quot; with no RAL number and no gloss\nlevel. Four matt 7016M windows beside a door of unstated shade, on the same elevation, is the\nsort of thing that gets noticed after it is installed.\n- JLL also asked Bradford Watts for cladding over the first floor windows. Mark never passed that\nto us and our quote says nothing about it either way - it reads as neither in nor out. Those are\nthe three first-floor windows we quoted in April, so it is worth knowing whether it is coming.\n- Nobody has given Bradford Watts a lead time. JLL asked them to shorten theirs and to finish by\nthe end of September. Our quotation does not mention one.\n The estimating log still shows this as &quot;Sent to ADAM&quot; and carries no deadline, which is correct -\nthe client has never given one. The 27/08 on the board is our own validity, not theirs.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential"
