   "subject": "Vesuvius - I was wrong, BSW do have it. The 60 minute door enquiry is written and needs sending today",
   "body": "Adam,\n Two things on Vesuvius. The first is me correcting myself; the second is the one\nthat still needs doing before Thursday.\n 1. THE RFQ DID REACH BSW - I WAS WRONG, AND I HAVE CHECKED IT PROPERLY THIS TIME\n\n You said it was sorted and sent after documents were removed. It was, and I can\nnow show it rather than take your word for it.\n Gintare sent three times. Only the first two bounced, and they were the SAME zip -\n28.5 MiB, which encodes to the 39 MB the bounce quotes against BSW's 36 MB cap.\nThe 15:22 attempt was a rebuilt zip of 19.9 MiB, about 27 MB as a message, and no\nbounce ever came back for it. I diffed the two attachments side by side.\n The four files dropped to get under the cap were 106B site context plan, 201O\nground floor plan, 202O first floor plan and 209O orthographic imaging - all\ngeneral background, none of it glazing information. BSW hold all nineteen of the\ndocuments that matter, including the window schedule 222P, the door schedule 221P\nand the NBS specification. That is actually a better enquiry than the one that went\non 27/07, which carried ten of the fifty-five files and was missing all three of\nthose. Whoever rebuilt that zip dropped exactly the right four files.\n So there is nothing to re-send, and my note this afternoon telling you it needed\nre-sending today was wrong. I had two bounces and three sends and assumed the\nthird failed like the other two.\n 2. THE 60 MINUTE DOORS - THE LETTER IS NOW WRITTEN\n This is REQ-8, open since Sunday, and it is the one with money on it. Nothing about\nthe BSW enquiry closes it, because that enquiry EXCLUDES fire-rated leaves and\ndoorsets unless BSW can certify them. Their return will come back with a hole\nexactly where the money is.\n The specification is not ambiguous - JHA NBS Section 2 clause L20 carries four\nseparate 60 minute door clauses, including &quot;60 Min Door installed in curtain wall&quot;,\nand the door schedule 221P agrees on every external type. We have the 2no doors in\nat GBP 4,683.56 as standard Senior SPD150, which is the wrong product family, and\nthe welfare screen at GBP 8,377.50 plus the office entrance screen at GBP 41,000.00\nboth carry doors inside them. That is GBP 49,377.50 - about 45% of the budget -\nsitting on SF52 screens whose doors have to be fire rated, and SF52 is not a fire\nrated system.\n I have written the enquiry so that sending it is a two-minute job:\n outputs\\Vesuvius Way - RFQ to Aluminium Fire Systems (draft, send today).txt\n It goes to Chris Wall, cc Charlie Skipp, lists the attachments, sets out five door\ntypes with sizes and ironmongery from 221P, asks for a rate per type so the counts\ncan flex, and asks for a return by 12:00 Thursday. AFS turned Gordon Court round in\ntwo days - enquired 07/07, quoted 09/07 at 11:02 - so they can still make it if it\ngoes today. I cannot send it myself; it needs Gintare or Steve.\n THREE THINGS I COULD NOT SETTLE MYSELF\n The package splits two ways and REQ-8 did not say so. AFS are aluminium fire\nscreens, so they cover the doors inside the curtain wall and the two internal\nPyroStop screens. The 60 minute insulated STEEL-CORE doors - fire escape, vision\npanel, louvred - are a steel doorset scope. Gintare sent a steel-door enquiry at\n15:31 naming drawing 2024/055/127 and the D.04 louvre door, but our copy of that\nemail shows no recipient at all, and nothing has come back. Worth thirty seconds\nof Gintare's time to confirm where it went.\n L20 and the door schedule both demand U-value 1.2 W/m2K on doors they also require\nto be 60 minute fire rated. I have asked AFS whether that is achievable. If it is\nnot, that is a conflict inside JHA's own specification and it is theirs to resolve,\nnot something we should quietly price around.\n L20 tells the reader to refer to drawing 2024-055-114, &quot;Building 01 Fire Plan&quot;,\nbefore any order is placed. It is not in the 55-file tender pack. It is the document\nthat would tell us which doors are 60 minute and where, so it is worth asking\nStaniforth for it.\n WHERE THE JOB STANDS\n GBP 110,551.98 ex VAT, benchmark only, no supplier quote held, nothing issued to\nStaniforth. Expect it high - the calibration log runs +10.4% on average and the\nlarge-unit band ran +35% on St Mary's, and this job is mostly large curtain wall.\nThe Senior fabricator problem is still open underneath all of it: the pack is\nentirely Senior and none of BSW, Aplus or Bellview make it.\n Also for the file, so nobody prices them by accident: Building 03 is not ours - its\ndoors are acoustic steel with two big roller shutters - and neither is the switch\nroom roller shutter on 221P. Both should be named in the exclusions when anything\ngoes to Staniforth.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error."
