   "attachments": 0,
   "body": "Mary,\n\n Where did you get the CN Glass info from?\n\n Kind regards, \n\n Adam Butcher \n Commercial Director \n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive \n Bradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n\n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Locks Ltd. If you are not the intended recipient of this email, you must neither take any action based upon its contents, nor copy or show it to anyone. Please contact the sender if you believe you have received this email in error.\n\n From: Mary Grace <mary@fensterglazing.com>\n Sent: 27 July 2026 9:23 AM\n To: Adam <adam@fensterglazing.com>; Marketing <marketing@fensterglazing.com>\n Subject: Stoke Park School (Borras) - Aplus 17644 final glass sizes are 46 panes / 25.6m2 more than the glass quotes cover \n\n Aplus issued the final glass sizes for job 17644 on Friday afternoon (Gintare forwarded them to Steve and Paul, cc you, 24/07 16:33).\n I have reconciled that list against the glass quotes on file. The final list is bigger than either quote covers, and the frames land on 03/08 unglazed - so this needs checking before the glass order goes out.\n HEADLINE\n Aplus final list: 170 panes to order, 130.81 m2.\n Vetroseal quote 064542 (01/07): 124 panes, 105.24 m2, GBP 12,012.88 net.\n Short by 46 panes / 25.57 m2 - about 24% more glass than is quoted.\n 1. WHAT IS MISSING\n Aplus gives three panes per window bay on most types (refs A1 / A4 / A8, and A1 / A5 on Type G). The schedule the quotes were priced from is one pane short on each. The pane absent every time is A1 - the roughly 391mm high toplight, 1041-1049 wide.\n Type A: 9 panes needed, 6 quoted Type B: 12 needed, 8 quoted Type C: 60 needed, 40 quoted Type D: 6 needed, 4 quoted Type F: 24 needed, 16 quoted Type G: 8 needed, 4 quoted Door Type B1 (D02) and B2 (D04): head pane missing on each Door Type C (D03): 3 panes, not on the quote at all Types E, H, J1, J2 and Door Types A and D: match 2. A MAKE-UP THAT IS NOT PRICED\n Aplus needs 9 panes at 32mm (8.33 m2) - the door head and transom panes. Vetroseal quoted every single line as 8.8L-16-4T, which is 28.8mm. The 32mm units need their own make-up and their own rate.\n Door leaf sizes have also moved: Aplus now calls for 749 x 2059, the quote is priced on 785 x 1934.\n 3. MONEY\n Vetroseal's own rate on this quote is GBP 110.00/m2 goods, plus the energy surcharge at GBP 0.13/kg (GBP 4.15/m2 here) - GBP 114.15/m2 all in.\n At that rate the full final list is about GBP 14,930 net against the GBP 12,012.88 quoted - roughly GBP 2,920 more, before whatever the 32mm make-up adds.\n CN Glass quoted the same make-up at GBP 60/m2 inc energy on 01/07 (Steve's thread with Martin Gregory), plus GBP 10/m2 if the inner leaf goes to 6mm toughened softcoat. The full final list at that rate is about GBP 7,850 - some GBP 7,000 below Vetroseal.\n Our price to Borras is GBP 104,660.17 ex VAT (pricing doc rev 15/07) with the glass inside the unit rates, so any increase comes straight off the margin.\n 4. DATES\n The Aplus sheet shows delivery 03/08/2026 - a week today. Frames are unglazed, supply only, so the glass is ours to order and ours to programme.\n Vetroseal 064542 is dated 01/07, so its 30-day validity runs out this week.\n 5. WHAT I NEED CONFIRMED\n 1. Which glass supplier holds this order, and that it is being placed against the 24/07 Aplus list rather than the earlier schedule.\n\n 2. The make-up for the nine 32mm door panes.\n\n 3. Whether the CN Glass rate is being used - on these areas the gap is around GBP 7,000.\n\n Five panes on the Aplus list are marked &quot;DO NOT ORDER - Unglazed&quot;. Those are the aluminium infill panels and I have excluded them from the 170.\n Full reconciliation attached - summary, per-type comparison, the complete Aplus list and the Vetroseal lines side by side:\n outputs\\Stoke Park School - Glass Sizes vs Quoted Glass (check).xlsx\n One caveat on the detail: pane sizes drifted a few millimetres between the earlier schedule and the final list, so which individual pane is missing is my reading of the sizes. The totals - 170 against 124 - are firm.\n SYSTEM NOTE FOR ZAC\n The poller re-queued three already-handled emails this morning. Microsoft's message ids are scoped to the Outlook folder a message sits in, so anything filed or moved comes back looking like new mail. Fixed: it now also keys on sender, subject and received time, seeded from the queue history. Nothing else was affected.\n Kind regards,\n Mary Grace \n Estimator\n 01908 429200 \n 97-98 Alston Drive\nBradwell Abbey, MK13 9HF \n www.fensterglazing.com \n\n This email and any attachments to it may be confidential and are intended solely for the use of the individual to whom it is addressed. Any views or opinions expressed are solely those of the author and do not necessarily represent those of Fenster Glazing & Lo"
